are placement | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-E004 | Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission time across training job types | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-E005 | Implement admin-defined preemption policy for higher-priority training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-E006 | Surface queue position, quota consumption, and admission state for pending jobs in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-E007 | Prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes for training job placement | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n\n`epic_count` counts main-plan epics (7). Branch epics (7, below) are plan documents\nattached to the gating investigation, not standalone issues.\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\nMain plan (arrows point from dependency to dependent):\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[RHAISTRAT-9005-E001 gang admission investigation] --> E006[RHAISTRAT-9005-E006 Dashboard visibility]\n    E004[RHAISTRAT-9005-E004 GPU quota at admission] --> E006\n    E002[RHAISTRAT-9005-E002 preemption semantics investigation] --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9005-E005 preemption policy]\n    E003[RHAISTRAT-9005-E003 topology maturity investigation] --> E007[RHAISTRAT-9005-E007 topology-aware placement]\n    E001 --> E007\n```\n\nBranch epics are excluded from the main-plan critical path. Main-plan critical\npath length: 2 (e.g. E001 → E006).\n\n## Conditional Decomposition Branches\n\nOpen Question 1 (\"do Kueue's current gang-admission semantics satisfy HLR-1 at\ntarget scale, or is scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue needed?\") has two bounded\noutcomes, and the strategy itself states the answer \"changes the shape of most\nimplementation work\". The admission implementation is therefore decomposed into\nconditional branches gated by E001:\n\n- **Branch A — Kueue semantics sufficient**: configuration and validation of\n  Kueue-native all-or-nothing admission (`waitForPodsReady`) for PyTorchJob and\n  RayJob queues, plus Training Operator conformance work.\n- **Branch B — scheduler-plugin work required**: the coscheduling scheduler\n  plugin is not in the platform inventory (architecture context ships no\n  scheduler plugins; Volcano is explicitly not shipped), so this branch carries\n  the full new-component onboarding chain (repo-onboarding ∥ license-validation\n  → konflux-onboarding ∥ integration implementation → Training Operator\n  adaptation).\n\nBranch epic files:\n\n| File | Branch | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Dependencies |\n|------|--------|-------|------|------|----------|--------------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008.md | A | Enable and validate Kueue-native gang admission for training queues | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E009.md | A | Training Operator conformance with Kueue-native gang admission at scale | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E008.md | B | Midstream repo onboarding for the coscheduling scheduler plugin | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E009.md | B | License validation for the coscheduling scheduler plugin dependency tree | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E010.md | B | Konflux onboarding for the coscheduling scheduler plugin | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, BRANCH-B-E008 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E011.md | B | Integrate coscheduling-based gang admission for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, BRANCH-B-E009 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E012.md | B | Adapt Training Operator jobs to coscheduling-based gang admission | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, BRANCH-B-E011 |\n\nBranch DAG:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[RHAISTRAT-9005-E001] --> AE008[BRANCH-A-E008 Kueue gang admission config]\n    E001 --> AE009[BRANCH-A-E009 Training Operator conformance]\n    E001 --> BE008[BRANCH-B-E008 repo onboarding]\n    E001 --> BE009[BRANCH-B-E009 license validation]\n    BE008 --> BE010[BRANCH-B-E010 konflux onboarding]\n    BE009 --> BE011[BRANCH-B-E011 coscheduling integration]\n    BE011 --> BE012[BRANCH-B-E012 Training Operator adaptation]\n```\n\nNote: no edge BRANCH-B-E010 → BRANCH-B-E011 — konflux onboarding and the\nintegration implementation run in parallel (Rule 10); the coupling is enforced by\na \"build pipeline green\" acceptance criterion on the integration epic (Rule 25).\n\nThe two other open questions use true gates on main-plan epics rather than\nbranches: the preemption epic exists under either semantics outcome (E002 gates\nE005 with `rewrite`), and topology placement exists only under the maturity\noutcome (E003 gates E007 with `remove` — under the negative outcome HLR-5 is\ndeferred and no branch work exists, so a single gated main-plan epic is the\nfaithful representation).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E006 | Rule 3 | Admission-state and queue-position surfacing depends on which admission mechanism is selected; investigation outcome rewrites the Dashboard's data sources. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n| E004 → E006 | Rule 13 | Dashboard builds against the per-project quota model produced by the quota implementation (consumes its API/CR surface). |\n| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 | Preemption semantics (full eviction vs checkpoint-aware) determine the epic's scope/approach. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n| E003 → E007 | Rule 3 | Topology placement epic may not exist if Tech Preview discovery is not mature enough. True gate: `remove` (HLR-5 deferred). |\n| E001 → E007 | Rule 3 | Placement integrates with whichever admission mechanism is selected; outcome may rewrite integration approach. |\n| E001 → BRANCH-A-E008, BRANCH-A-E009 | Rule 3 | Branch existence determined by investigation outcome. True gate: `remove`. |\n| E001 → BRANCH-B-E008..E012 | Rule 3 | Branch existence determined by investigation outcome. True gate: `remove`. |\n| BRANCH-B-E008 → BRANCH-B-E010 | Rule 5 | repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding always serial (pipeline needs repo). |\n| BRANCH-B-E009 → BRANCH-B-E011 | Rule 9 | license-validation → general implementation serial (license failures change dependencies/approach). |\n| BRANCH-B-E010 ∥ BRANCH-B-E011 | Rule 10 | Konflux config is independent of integration code; no blocking edge either direction. \"Build pipeline green\" AC on the integration epic enforces the coupling. |\n| BRANCH-B-E011 → BRANCH-B-E012 | Rule 12/13 | Training Operator adaptation builds against the gang-admission mechanism the integration produces. |\n| E001, E002, E003, E004 (roots, no edges between) | Rules 14/15 | Quota enforcement (E004) is Kueue-native and independent of the gang-semantics outcome (scheduler-plugin question concerns gang semantics, not queueing/quota, which stays in Kueue). Investigations are independent of each other and of quota work. |\n| BRANCH-A-E008 ∥ BRANCH-A-E009 | Rule 14 | Different repos (Kueue config vs training-operator), no shared artifacts. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n|-----|----------|-------|\n| HLR-1 (all-or-nothing admission) | P0 | E001 (investigation); BRANCH-A-E008 + BRANCH-A-E009 (outcome A) or BRANCH-B-E008/E009/E010/E011/E012 (outcome B) |\n| HLR-2 (per-project GPU quota at admission) | P0 | E004 (quota enforcement; all-or-nothing admission of quota-admitted jobs is validated by the HLR-1 branch work) |\n| HLR-3 (Dashboard queue/quota/admission visibility) | P1 | E006 |\n| HLR-4 (preemption per admin policy) | P1 | E002 (investigation), E005 |\n| HLR-5 (topology-aligned placement) | P2 | E003 (investigation), E007 |\n\nAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table,\n  Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then), or NFRs. Team ownership was