{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f560ec92-7237-4688-8abd-4e2f6fac7096","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9903513e2f2ed93f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-o2g1ekyv/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E001.md","content":"# Validate Kueue gang-admission semantics at target scale for PyTorchJob and RayJob\n\n## Description\n\nResolves the strategy's first open question: whether Kueue's current gang-admission\nsemantics (all-or-nothing admission via `waitForPodsReady`) actually satisfy the\nall-or-nothing requirement for multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads at the\nplatform's target scale, or whether scheduler-plugin work (e.g. a coscheduling\nplugin) beyond Kueue is required. The outcome determines which implementation\npath the rest of the queue-aware scheduling work takes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Reproduce the piecemeal-admission failure mode described in the strategy\n  (partial GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods, timeout deaths of\n  partially scheduled jobs) with multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads\n  under Kueue admission.\n- Exercise Kueue's all-or-nothing admission (`waitForPodsReady`) for both job\n  types at representative scale (job sizes and queue depth matching customer\n  fleets, e.g. 16-GPU multi-node jobs), including contention scenarios where\n  multiple teams' jobs compete for the same GPU pool.\n- Determine whether admission semantics hold at target scale: no partial GPU\n  occupation during pending admission, correct release of quota on eviction or\n  timeout, and re-admission behavior after preemption or failure.\n- Produce a written recommendation with a clear decision: (A) Kueue-native\n  semantics are sufficient, or (B) scheduler-plugin work (e.g. coscheduling)\n  beyond Kueue is required — including the evidence (metrics, logs, test\n  results) supporting the decision.\n- Identify any Kueue configuration or integration gaps discovered along the way\n  that either outcome would need to address.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A test harness exists that submits multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads\n  through Kueue queues and observes admission behavior at representative scale.\n- For each job type, it is demonstrated and documented whether pending jobs hold\n  zero GPUs until all pods can be admitted (pass) or occupy GPUs partially\n  while waiting (fail).\n- A written recommendation selects outcome A or B with supporting evidence and\n  identifies the concrete consequences for the admission, quota, preemption,\n  topology, and Dashboard work.\n- If outcome B, the recommendation identifies the scheduler-plugin approach to\n  carry forward (component to onboard, integration points with Kueue queueing).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): this investigation determines whether Kueue-native semantics\n  satisfy the all-or-nothing admission requirement or whether scheduler-plugin\n  work is needed.\n\n## Open Questions Addressed\n\n- Strategy Open Question 1 (Kueue gang-admission semantics vs scheduler-plugin\n  work at target scale).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42047,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877e8074d5525529","agent_id":"a1856a53627dd173a","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"ed0fc6a5-7e0c-4f25-b2bd-1d42c4661159","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:05:05.058Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
