ed (duration, size, throughput impact).\n- A written recommendation selects the preemption semantics and states what the\n  preemption policy implementation must support.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P1): this investigation determines the semantics the admin-defined\n  preemption policy must implement.\n\n## Open Questions Addressed\n\n- Strategy Open Question 3 (preemption semantics: full eviction with requeue vs\n  checkpoint-aware graceful preemption; checkpoint overhead benchmark).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42903,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877e8074d5525529","agent_id":"a1856a53627dd173a","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"cc51fc43-0882-427e-a115-a68190544c41","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:05:20.612Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
