{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-dcb1ba19-a0a0-445a-bf8c-5a276b9e6a24","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-955b6f8434bc44a5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-o2g1ekyv/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E004.md","content":"# Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission time across training job types\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission time, so that a project's\npending training jobs (PyTorchJob and RayJob) cannot consume more GPUs than the\nproject's quota allows, regardless of job type. Enforcement happens at admission\n(pending jobs hold no resources), building on the platform's Kueue-based\nqueueing layer.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the per-project GPU quota model on top of the existing Kueue\n  queueing primitives (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model), mapping projects to\n  quota boundaries so quota is shared across PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads\n  within a project.\n- Implement/administer the quota configuration so that admission-time checks\n  reject or delay jobs that would exceed a project's GPU quota.\n- Ensure quota is correctly released when jobs complete, fail, or are evicted,\n  including under the all-or-nothing admission semantics delivered by the\n  gang-admission work (the two share Kueue queueing configuration; coordinate\n  the configuration changes rather than duplicating them).\n- Verify quota accounting across mixed fleets of PyTorchJob and RayJob\n  workloads in the same project, including concurrent multi-node jobs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A project submitting training jobs whose combined GPU requests exceed its\n  quota has the excess jobs held pending at admission (zero GPUs occupied),\n  measured by pending workloads and GPU allocation per project over the test\n  window.\n- Quota is enforced uniformly across PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads in the\n  same project (a RayJob cannot bypass a quota saturated by PyTorchJobs, and\n  vice versa).\n- Quota is fully released within a bounded time after job completion, failure,\n  or eviction, measured by post-job GPU allocation returning to the pre-job\n  level.\n- A pending job admitted when quota frees up starts with all its pods (no\n  partial occupation while waiting), consistent with the all-or-nothing\n  admission requirement.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): per-project GPU quota enforced at admission time across training\n  job types (PyTorchJob, RayJob).\n- Supports HLR-1 (P0): quota-enforced admission keeps pending jobs\n  resource-free; all-or-nothing admission itself is delivered by the\n  gang-admission work selected by the admission-semantics investigation.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44015,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877e8074d5525529","agent_id":"a1856a53627dd173a","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"10bc43d4-3104-40a3-bdbd-52f143e11804","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:05:51.368Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
