{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9e4e7f30-2e25-437d-8596-734dd5eedff6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdf7b3f8dfc9c9e8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-o2g1ekyv/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E005.md","content":"# Implement admin-defined preemption policy for higher-priority training workloads\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers preemption of lower-priority training workloads by higher-priority ones\naccording to an admin-defined policy. The concrete preemption semantics (full\neviction with requeue, or checkpoint-aware graceful preemption) are determined\nby the preemption-semantics investigation; this epic implements the policy\nmachinery on the platform's Kueue-based queueing layer once that outcome is\nknown.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement admin-defined preemption policy configuration on the queueing\n  layer, allowing administrators to express which workloads may preempt which\n  (workload priority and queue boundaries).\n- Implement the preemption semantics selected by the preemption-semantics\n  investigation: full eviction with requeue, checkpoint-aware graceful\n  preemption, or a policy-configurable mix — including the requeue/admission\n  path for preempted jobs.\n- Ensure preempted quota is released promptly so the preempting workload can be\n  admitted, and preempted jobs re-enter the queue rather than being lost.\n- If checkpoint-aware graceful preemption is selected, coordinate with the\n  Training Operator on checkpoint/suspend support (the operator-side work will\n  be scoped when the semantics decision lands; this epic covers the\n  queueing-layer policy and lifecycle).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- An administrator can define a preemption policy, and a higher-priority\n  workload submitted against a saturated GPU pool causes a lower-priority\n  workload to be preempted per that policy, measured by admission events and GPU\n  reallocation within the test window.\n- Preempted workloads are requeued (and, if the selected semantics require it,\n  resumed from checkpoint) rather than lost, measured by their eventual\n  re-admission.\n- GPU quota held by the preempted workload is released to the preempting\n  workload within a bounded time, measured by GPU allocation transitions.\n- Preemption behavior matches the semantics recommended by the\n  preemption-semantics investigation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P1): higher-priority workloads can preempt lower-priority ones\n  according to an admin-defined policy.\n\n## Dependencies and Gates\n\n- Gated by the preemption-semantics investigation (customer-requirements\n  reconciliation plus checkpoint-overhead benchmark): if the outcome differs\n  from the assumed approach, this epic's scope is rewritten rather than\n  removed — preemption is delivered under either semantics.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44727,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877e8074d5525529","agent_id":"a1856a53627dd173a","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"28b81194-e1af-4bb4-aa78-b45e45d7e20c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:06:06.834Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
