{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-51093690-5be5-4ed9-812c-7d1e48e927b1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd583fbfe6ee511d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-o2g1ekyv/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E006.md","content":"# Surface queue position, quota consumption, and admission state for pending jobs in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nExtends the Dashboard so users can see, for their pending training jobs: queue\nposition, per-project GPU quota consumption, and admission state (pending,\nadmitted, preempted/requeued). The Dashboard reads Kubernetes CRs and queueing\nmetrics and owns no data plane, consistent with its existing distributed\nworkload status integration.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add queue-aware scheduling status to the Dashboard's distributed workload\n  views: pending jobs show their queue position and admission state.\n- Surface per-project GPU quota consumption (used vs. quota) alongside pending\n  jobs, based on the quota model delivered by the per-project GPU quota\n  enforcement work.\n- Display admission state transitions relevant to gang admission and\n  preemption (pending as a whole unit, admitted, preempted and requeued), based\n  on the admission mechanism selected by the gang-admission semantics\n  investigation.\n- Respect project-scoped visibility (users see queue/quota state for their own\n  projects), consistent with the Dashboard's existing RBAC model.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user with a pending multi-node training job sees its queue position in the\n  Dashboard, measured by comparing the displayed position with the queueing\n  layer's pending-workload ordering for the same job.\n- A user sees their project's GPU quota consumption (used and quota) alongside\n  pending jobs, measured against the actual allocation enforced by the\n  admission-time quota.\n- Admission state (pending, admitted, preempted/requeued) is displayed and\n  matches the workload's actual state, measured over a test run that exercises\n  pending → admitted and preemption → requeue transitions.\n- Users cannot see queue or quota state for projects they do not have access\n  to, measured by scoped-user checks.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): users can see queue position, quota consumption, and admission\n  state for their pending jobs in the Dashboard.\n\n## Dependencies and Gates\n\n- Gated by the gang-admission semantics investigation: the admission mechanism\n  selected (Kueue-native versus scheduler-plugin) determines which states and\n  data sources the Dashboard must surface; the outcome rewrites this epic's\n  data-source scope but the Dashboard visibility itself is delivered either way.\n- Builds against the per-project GPU quota model delivered by the quota\n  enforcement work (quota consumption display consumes that model).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45430,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877e8074d5525529","agent_id":"a1856a53627dd173a","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"7ff8b428-5b6a-49f5-84b7-339f8aaa7db3","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:06:22.538Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
