{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b870fd5c-1617-4112-a512-cd69bf87eaf0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8443dc3bbab34d38","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-o2g1ekyv/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E007.md","content":"# Prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes for training job placement\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers placement that prefers GPU-topology-aligned nodes for training jobs\nwhen the cluster exposes topology information (e.g. keeping a job's GPUs within\nNVLink domains), addressing the throughput loss customers report from\nmis-topologized placement. Only proceeds if the node topology discovery\nfoundation is judged mature enough for this release.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement a placement preference for training jobs that uses cluster topology\n  information (when exposed) to prefer topology-aligned node/GPU sets for a\n  job's pods.\n- Integrate the preference with the admission mechanism selected by the\n  gang-admission semantics investigation, so topology preference applies at\n  admission time without breaking all-or-nothing semantics.\n- Degrade gracefully on clusters that do not expose topology information:\n  placement falls back to the default behavior and the requirement's\n  \"can prefer\" semantics are preserved.\n- Validate placement quality (jobs land within aligned topology domains when\n  available) and the throughput benefit on representative multi-node GPU jobs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- On a cluster exposing topology information, admitted multi-node training jobs\n  are placed on topology-aligned node/GPU sets when such sets are available,\n  measured by comparing job pod placement against reported topology domains.\n- On a cluster without topology information, jobs are admitted and placed via\n  the default behavior with no errors, measured by admission success rate\n  matching the non-topology baseline.\n- Topology preference does not break all-or-nothing admission (no partial\n  admission while waiting for a topology-aligned set), measured by GPU\n  occupation of pending jobs remaining zero.\n- A representative multi-node job shows no cross-domain GPU placement where an\n  in-domain placement was available, measured over the validation run.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P2): job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the\n  cluster exposes topology information.\n\n## Dependencies and Gates\n\n- Gated by the topology-discovery maturity investigation: if the Tech Preview\n  discovery foundation is not mature enough for this release, this epic is\n  removed and the requirement is deferred (documented limitation).\n- Also depends on the gang-admission semantics investigation's outcome, which\n  determines the admission mechanism the placement preference integrates with.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46128,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877e8074d5525529","agent_id":"a1856a53627dd173a","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"4b37e720-71e9-4750-b61f-d83bc23bd69b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:06:37.279Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
