{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c91c2f87-7bf5-41ec-abe2-ba6a26cd361d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9208178551efe57a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-o2g1ekyv/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008.md","content":"# Enable and validate Kueue-native gang admission for training queues\n\n## Description\n\nBranch A (Kueue's current gang-admission semantics are sufficient): configures\nand validates all-or-nothing admission via Kueue for multi-node training\nworkloads — PyTorchJob and RayJob — so a job holds zero GPUs until all of its\npods can be admitted, eliminating the piecemeal occupation and partial-timeout\nfailures described in the strategy.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Configure the platform's Kueue queueing layer so training queues admit\n  multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads all-or-nothing (gang admission via\n  waitForPodsReady semantics), consistent with the validation performed in the\n  gang-admission semantics investigation.\n- Cover both job types' admission paths (PyTorchJob via the training-operator\n  Kueue integration, RayJob via the Kuberay/Kueue integration).\n- Tune admission behavior at target scale per the investigation's findings\n  (queue depth, contention, timeout and requeue handling for jobs that cannot\n  be fully admitted).\n- Coordinate with the per-project GPU quota configuration, which shares the\n  same Kueue queueing objects, so quota and gang semantics compose correctly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A pending multi-node PyTorchJob or RayJob holds zero GPUs while waiting for\n  its remaining pods, measured by per-job GPU allocation during the pending\n  window across a representative-scale test run.\n- A job that cannot be fully admitted within its timeout is rejected/evicted as\n  a whole unit with its quota released, measured by no lingering partial\n  allocation after timeout.\n- Under contention (multiple teams' jobs competing for one GPU pool), admission\n  remains all-or-nothing and quota accounting is correct, measured by admission\n  events and GPU allocation over the contention window.\n- Behavior matches the gang-admission semantics investigation's recommendation\n  (the configuration implements the validated semantics, not an assumption).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing; no partial\n  GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods.\n\n## Branch Context\n\n- Branch A of the gang-admission semantics investigation: applies when\n  Kueue-native semantics are judged sufficient at target scale. If the\n  investigation instead requires scheduler-plugin work, this epic is removed and\n  the coscheduling integration path applies.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46794,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877e8074d5525529","agent_id":"a1856a53627dd173a","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"260cde1d-37ae-44f5-8431-6bff096b6535","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:06:54.478Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
