in its timeout is evicted as a\n  whole unit with quota released, measured by no lingering partial allocation\n  after timeout.\n- The Konflux build pipeline for the scheduler plugin is green for the revision\n  being integrated, measured by the pipeline run status.\n- Queueing and per-project quota continue to be enforced correctly with the\n  plugin active, measured by admission events and per-project GPU allocation\n  over the test window.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing; no partial\n  GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods.\n\n## Branch Context\n\n- Branch B of the gang-admission semantics investigation: applies when\n  scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue is required. If Kueue-native semantics are\n  sufficient, this epic is removed. Serial after license validation (license\n  failures would change the dependency set and the approach); parallel with the\n  Konflux onboarding — the coupling is enforced by the green-pipeline\n  acceptance criterion above, not a dependency edge.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49834,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877e8074d5525529","agent_id":"a1856a53627dd173a","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"76bb3ef3-82f4-4e0b-8667-afdf2366ae2c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:08:04.251Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
