{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a94396b3-ad7a-4669-8307-cdb1cfa091e3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b53f5bc3ba7ca592","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-o2g1ekyv/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E012.md","content":"# Adapt Training Operator jobs to coscheduling-based gang admission\n\n## Description\n\nBranch B (scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue is required): adapts the Training\nOperator's PyTorchJob handling to the coscheduling-based gang admission\nmechanism, so multi-node PyTorchJobs participate in scheduler-level pod groups\ninstead of relying on Kueue-native suspend-based admission semantics, and\nremain correct under preemption and requeue.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Adapt PyTorchJob pod generation and job lifecycle handling (launch topology,\n  suspend/resume semantics, status reporting) to participate in the\n  coscheduling pod-group mechanism integrated into the platform's scheduling\n  stack.\n- Ensure job pods carry the group membership the scheduler plugin requires and\n  that the operator reacts correctly to whole-group admission, eviction, and\n  requeue events.\n- Validate multi-node PyTorchJob behavior at representative scale under the\n  plugin-based mechanism, including contention and preemption transitions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Multi-node PyTorchJobs are admitted as whole units (launcher and all workers)\n  under the coscheduling mechanism, measured by admission/scheduling events\n  showing no partial pod sets running while a job is pending.\n- A preempted or evicted PyTorchJob is requeued and re-admitted as a whole\n  unit and completes training correctly, measured by job success over a test\n  run exercising those transitions.\n- No Training Operator defects remain that break group-based all-or-nothing\n  admission at representative scale, measured by the validation suite passing\n  at the scale exercised in the gang-admission semantics investigation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing — Training\n  Operator side (PyTorchJob) of the scheduler-plugin admission path.\n- HLR-2 (P0, supporting): PyTorchJobs correctly enter and release per-project\n  GPU quota through the group-based admission, completion, and requeue.\n\n## Branch Context\n\n- Branch B of the gang-admission semantics investigation: applies when\n  scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue is required. If Kueue-native semantics are\n  sufficient, this epic is removed. Serial after the coscheduling integration\n  work — the operator adaptation builds against the group mechanism it\n  produces.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50581,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877e8074d5525529","agent_id":"a1856a53627dd173a","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"55d3c982-edf1-499e-a1a7-c031dce8da73","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:08:19.161Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
