n67\tconditional branches gated by E001:\n68\t\n69\t- **Branch A — Kueue semantics sufficient**: configuration and validation of\n70\t  Kueue-native all-or-nothing admission (`waitForPodsReady`) for PyTorchJob and\n71\t  RayJob queues, plus Training Operator conformance work.\n72\t- **Branch B — scheduler-plugin work required**: the coscheduling scheduler\n73\t  plugin is not in the platform inventory (architecture context ships no\n74\t  scheduler plugins; Volcano is explicitly not shipped), so this branch carries\n75\t  the full new-component onboarding chain (repo-onboarding ∥ license-validation\n76\t  → konflux-onboarding ∥ integration implementation → Training Operator\n77\t  adaptation).\n78\t\n79\tBranch epic files:\n80\t\n81\t| File | Branch | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Dependencies |\n82\t|------|--------|-------|------|------|----------|--------------|\n83\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008.md | A | Enable and validate Kueue-native gang admission for training queues | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n84\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E009.md | A | Training Operator conformance with Kueue-native gang admission at scale | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n85\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E008.md | B | Midstream repo onboarding for the coscheduling scheduler plugin | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n86\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E009.md | B | License validation for the coscheduling scheduler plugin dependency tree | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n87\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E010.md | B | Konflux onboarding for the coscheduling scheduler plugin | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, BRANCH-B-E008 |\n88\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E011.md | B | Integrate coscheduling-based gang admission for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, BRANCH-B-E009 |\n89\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E012.md | B | Adapt Training Operator jobs to coscheduling-based gang admission | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, BRANCH-B-E011 |\n90\t\n91\tBranch DAG:\n92\t\n93\t```mermaid\n94\tgraph TD\n95\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9005-E001] --> AE008[BRANCH-A-E008 Kueue gang admission config]\n96\t    E001 --> AE009[BRANCH-A-E009 Training Operator conformance]\n97\t    E001 --> BE008[BRANCH-B-E008 repo onboarding]\n98\t    E001 --> BE009[BRANCH-B-E009 license validation]\n99\t    BE008 --> BE010[BRANCH-B-E010 konflux onboarding]\n100\t    BE009 --> BE011[BRANCH-B-E011 coscheduling integration]\n101\t    BE011 --> BE012[BRANCH-B-E012 Training Operator adaptation]\n102\t```\n103\t\n104\tNote: no edge BRANCH-B-E010 → BRANCH-B-E011 — konflux onboarding and the\n105\tintegration implementation run in parallel (Rule 10); the coupling is enforced by\n106\ta \"build pipeline green\" acceptance criterion on the integration epic (Rule 25).\n107\t\n108\tThe two other open questions use true gates on main-plan epics rather than\n109\tbranches: the preemption epic exists under either semantics outcome (E002 gates\n110\tE005 with `rewrite`), and topology placement exists only under the maturity\n111\toutcome (E003 gates E007 with `remove` — under the negative outcome HLR-5 is\n112\tdeferred and no branch work exists, so a single gated main-plan epic is the\n113\tfaithful representation).\n114\t\n115\t## DAG Justification\n116\t\n117\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n118\t|------|------|-----------|\n119\t| E001 → E006 | Rule 3 | Admission-state and queue-position surfacing depends on which admission mechanism is selected; investigation outcome rewrites the Dashboard's data sources. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n120\t| E004 → E006 | Rule 13 | Dashboard builds against the per-project quota model produced by the quota implementation (consumes its API/CR surface). |\n121\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 | Preemption semantics (full eviction vs checkpoint-aware) determine the epic's scope/approach. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n122\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 3 | Topology placement epic may not exist if Tech Preview discovery is not mature enough. True gate: `remove` (HLR-5 deferred). |\n123\t| E001 → E007 | Rule 3 | Placement integrates with whichever admission mechanism is selected; outcome may rewrite integration approach. |\n124\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E008, BRANCH-A-E009 | Rule 3 | Branch existence determined by investigation outcome. True gate: `remove`. |\n125\t| E001 → BRANCH-B-E008..E012 | Rule 3 | Branch existence determined by investigation outcome. True gate: `remove`. |\n126\t| BRANCH-B-E008 → BRANCH-B-E010 | Rule 5 | repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding always serial (pipeline needs repo). |\n127\t| BRANCH-B-E009 → BRANCH-B-E011 | Rule 9 | license-validation → general implementation serial (license failures change dependencies/approach). |\n128\t| BRANCH-B-E010 ∥ BRANCH-B-E011 | Rule 10 | Konflux config is independent of integration code; no blocking edge either direction. \"Build pipeline green\" AC on the integration epic enforces the coupling. |\n129\t| BRANCH-B-E011 → BRANCH-B-E012 | Rule 12/13 | Training Operator adaptation builds against the gang-admission mechanism the integration produces. |\n130\t| E001, E002, E003, E004 (roots, no edges between) | Rules 14/15 | Quota enforcement (E004) is Kueue-native and independent of the gang-semantics outcome (scheduler-plugin question concerns gang semantics, not queueing/quota, which stays in Kueue). Investigations are independent of each other and of quota work. |\n131\t| BRANCH-A-E008 ∥ BRANCH-A-E009 | Rule 14 | Different repos (Kueue config vs training-operator), no shared artifacts. |\n132\t\n133\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n134\t\n135\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n136\t|-----|----------|-------|\n137\t| HLR-1 (all-or-nothing admission) | P0 | E001 (investigation); BRANCH-A-E008 + BRANCH-A-E009 (outcome A) or BRANCH-B-E008/E009/E010/E011/E012 (outcome B) |\n138\t| HLR-2 (per-project GPU quota at admission) | P0 | E004 (quota enforcement; all-or-nothing admission of quota-admitted jobs is validated by the HLR-1 branch work) |\n139\t| HLR-3 (Dashboard queue/quota/admission visibility) | P1 | E006 |\n140\t| HLR-4 (preemption per admin policy) | P1 | E002 (investigation), E005 |\n141\t| HLR-5 (topology-aligned placement) | P2 | E003 (investigation), E007 |\n142\t\n143\tAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements.\n144\t\n145\t## Health Warnings\n146\t\n147\t- **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table,\n148\t  Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then), or NFRs. Team ownership was inferred\n149\t  from architecture context; epic acceptance criteria were derived from HLRs and\n150\t  may need refinement against the strategy author's intent.\n151\t- **Priority inversion risk**: HLR-5 (topology-aligned placement) is P2 despite\n152\t  the problem statement citing \"significant throughput loss\" from mis-topologized\n153\t  placement. If field reports weigh heavily, consider raising it; it is also the\n154\t  requirement most at risk of deferral (Tech Preview dependency).\n155\t- **Scope trap**: HLR-5's acceptance depends on node topology discovery\n156\t  infrastructure that is only Tech Preview — building a P2 feature on Tech\n157\t  Preview foundations is a reliability risk; the maturity investigation (E003)\n158\t  gates it.\n159\t- **Shared config surface**: E004 (quota) and the branch admission epics both\n160\t  modify the same Kueue queueing objects (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue). Per Rule 15\n161\t  they run in parallel; merge conflicts are a coordination risk, not a\n162\t  dependency. Sequence the config PRs.\n163\t- **Preemption component boundary**: if E002 selects checkpoint-aware graceful\n164\t  preemption, the Training Operator likely needs checkpoint/suspend work beyond\n165\t  E005's Distributed Workloads scope; the gate is recorded as `rewrite` and a\n166\t  follow-up Training Operator epic should be scoped at that point.\n167\t- **Out-of-scope consistency**: GPU sharing/fractioning and multi-c