{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5eb99308e04afa3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E006\n3\ttitle: Surface queue position, quota consumption, and admission state for pending\n4\t  jobs in the Dashboard\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n6\tcomponent: Dashboard\n7\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E004\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue is required for gang admission,\n17\t    the Dashboard's data sources for queue position and admission state are rewritten\n18\t    to the plugin-based admission record; the visibility feature itself is still delivered.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 5\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Surface queue position, quota consumption, and admission state for pending jobs in the Dashboard\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tExtends the Dashboard so users can see, for their pending training jobs: queue\n41\tposition, per-project GPU quota consumption, and admission state (pending,\n42\tadmitted, preempted/requeued). The Dashboard reads Kubernetes CRs and queueing\n43\tmetrics and owns no data plane, consistent with its existing distributed\n44\tworkload status integration.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Add queue-aware scheduling status to the Dashboard's distributed workload\n49\t  views: pending jobs show their queue position and admission state.\n50\t- Surface per-project GPU quota consumption (used vs. quota) alongside pending\n51\t  jobs, based on the quota model delivered by the per-project GPU quota\n52\t  enforcement work.\n53\t- Display admission state transitions relevant to gang admission and\n54\t  preemption (pending as a whole unit, admitted, preempted and requeued), based\n55\t  on the admission mechanism selected by the gang-admission semantics\n56\t  investigation.\n57\t- Respect project-scoped visibility (users see queue/quota state for their own\n58\t  projects), consistent with the Dashboard's existing RBAC model.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- A user with a pending multi-node training job sees its queue position in the\n63\t  Dashboard, measured by comparing the displayed position with the queueing\n64\t  layer's pending-workload ordering for the same job.\n65\t- A user sees their project's GPU quota consumption (used and quota) alongside\n66\t  pending jobs, measured against the actual allocation enforced by the\n67\t  admission-time quota.\n68\t- Admission state (pending, admitted, preempted/requeued) is displayed and\n69\t  matches the workload's actual state, measured over a test run that exercises\n70\t  pending → admitted and preemption → requeue transitions.\n71\t- Users cannot see queue or quota state for projects they do not have access\n72\t  to, measured by scoped-user checks.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-3 (P1): users can see queue position, quota consumption, and admission\n77\t  state for their pending jobs in the Dashboard.\n78\t\n79\t## Dependencies and Gates\n80\t\n81\t- Gated by the gang-admission semantics investigation: the admission mechanism\n82\t  selected (Kueue-native versus scheduler-plugin) determines which states and\n83\t  data sources the Dashboard must surface; the outcome rewrites this epic's\n84\t  data-source scope but the Dashboard visibility itself is delivered either way.\n85\t- Builds against the per-project GPU quota model delivered by the quota\n86\t  enforcement work (quota consumption display consumes that model).\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99416dc38feb6afb","agent_id":"a2a7cb73cc5c9b3e4","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"f03c305f-13f0-460c-ad98-630fbf94d94a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:13:59.654Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5eb99308e04afa3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
