{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ce9fb4c12abc81","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E007\n3\ttitle: Prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes for training job placement\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If node topology discovery is not mature enough this release,\n16\t    HLR-5 is deferred and this epic is removed; the limitation is documented for customers.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 0\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 1\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes for training job placement\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tDelivers placement that prefers GPU-topology-aligned nodes for training jobs\n39\twhen the cluster exposes topology information (e.g. keeping a job's GPUs within\n40\tNVLink domains), addressing the throughput loss customers report from\n41\tmis-topologized placement. Only proceeds if the node topology discovery\n42\tfoundation is judged mature enough for this release.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Implement a placement preference for training jobs that uses cluster topology\n47\t  information (when exposed) to prefer topology-aligned node/GPU sets for a\n48\t  job's pods.\n49\t- Integrate the preference with the admission mechanism selected by the\n50\t  gang-admission semantics investigation, so topology preference applies at\n51\t  admission time without breaking all-or-nothing semantics.\n52\t- Degrade gracefully on clusters that do not expose topology information:\n53\t  placement falls back to the default behavior and the requirement's\n54\t  \"can prefer\" semantics are preserved.\n55\t- Validate placement quality (jobs land within aligned topology domains when\n56\t  available) and the throughput benefit on representative multi-node GPU jobs.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- On a cluster exposing topology information, admitted multi-node training jobs\n61\t  are placed on topology-aligned node/GPU sets when such sets are available,\n62\t  measured by comparing job pod placement against reported topology domains.\n63\t- On a cluster without topology information, jobs are admitted and placed via\n64\t  the default behavior with no errors, measured by admission success rate\n65\t  matching the non-topology baseline.\n66\t- Topology preference does not break all-or-nothing admission (no partial\n67\t  admission while waiting for a topology-aligned set), measured by GPU\n68\t  occupation of pending jobs remaining zero.\n69\t- A representative multi-node job shows no cross-domain GPU placement where an\n70\t  in-domain placement was available, measured over the validation run.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-5 (P2): job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the\n75\t  cluster exposes topology information.\n76\t\n77\t## Dependencies and Gates\n78\t\n79\t- Gated by the topology-discovery maturity investigation: if the Tech Preview\n80\t  discovery foundation is not mature enough for this release, this epic is\n81\t  removed and the requirement is deferred (documented limitation).\n82\t- Also depends on the gang-admission semantics investigation's outcome, which\n83\t  determines the admission mechanism the placement preference integrates with.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99416dc38feb6afb","agent_id":"a2a7cb73cc5c9b3e4","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"6af990d4-c1de-43f7-a833-4518c8022cad","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:14:00.792Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ce9fb4c12abc81","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
