{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83181a22af86d1ed","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E009\n3\ttitle: Training Operator conformance with Kueue-native gang admission at scale\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the gang-admission semantics investigation requires scheduler-plugin\n16\t    work beyond Kueue, this epic is removed and the Training Operator adaptation for\n17\t    coscheduling-based admission applies.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Training Operator conformance with Kueue-native gang admission at scale\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tBranch A (Kueue's current gang-admission semantics are sufficient): ensures the\n39\tTraining Operator's PyTorchJob handling conforms to queue-aware all-or-nothing\n40\tadmission at target scale — suspension, resume, and job-topology semantics must\n41\thold up when jobs are admitted as whole units through Kueue, including under\n42\tpreemption and requeue.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Validate PyTorchJob lifecycle behavior under Kueue-native gang admission at\n47\t  representative scale: job suspension while pending, full-unit admission,\n48\t  pod-spec conformance for gang scheduling, and correct handling of the job's\n49\t  replica topology (launcher/worker pods admitted together).\n50\t- Fix Training Operator defects surfaced by that validation (e.g. incorrect\n51\t  suspend/resume handling, pod mutations that break admission, stuck jobs after\n52\t  partial-node failures), staying within the operator's existing\n53\t  Kueue-integration model.\n54\t- Ensure preempted/requeued PyTorchJobs restart correctly through the\n55\t  operator's suspend path when workload queueing is enabled.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Multi-node PyTorchJobs are admitted as whole units (launcher and all workers)\n60\t  through Kueue queueing, measured by admission events showing no partial pod\n61\t  sets running while a job is pending.\n62\t- A suspended-then-resumed PyTorchJob (pending → admitted, and preempted →\n63\t  requeued → re-admitted) completes training correctly, measured by job success\n64\t  over a test run exercising those transitions.\n65\t- No Training Operator defects remain that break all-or-nothing admission at\n66\t  representative scale, measured by the validation suite passing at the scale\n67\t  exercised in the gang-admission semantics investigation.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing — Training\n72\t  Operator side (PyTorchJob) of the Kueue-native admission path.\n73\t- HLR-2 (P0, supporting): PyTorchJobs correctly enter and release per-project\n74\t  GPU quota through admission, completion, and requeue.\n75\t\n76\t## Branch Context\n77\t\n78\t- Branch A of the gang-admission semantics investigation: applies when\n79\t  Kueue-native semantics are judged sufficient. If the investigation instead\n80\t  requires scheduler-plugin work, this epic is removed and the operator\n81\t  adaptation for coscheduling-based admission applies.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99416dc38feb6afb","agent_id":"a2a7cb73cc5c9b3e4","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"d04dda54-7694-48ab-9743-fe5ccaf5a743","timestamp":"20