o whole-group admission, eviction, and\n52\t  requeue events.\n53\t- Validate multi-node PyTorchJob behavior at representative scale under the\n54\t  plugin-based mechanism, including contention and preemption transitions.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Multi-node PyTorchJobs are admitted as whole units (launcher and all workers)\n59\t  under the coscheduling mechanism, measured by admission/scheduling events\n60\t  showing no partial pod sets running while a job is pending.\n61\t- A preempted or evicted PyTorchJob is requeued and re-admitted as a whole\n62\t  unit and completes training correctly, measured by job success over a test\n63\t  run exercising those transitions.\n64\t- No Training Operator defects remain that break group-based all-or-nothing\n65\t  admission at representative scale, measured by the validation suite passing\n66\t  at the scale exercised in the gang-admission semantics investigation.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing — Training\n71\t  Operator side (PyTorchJob) of the scheduler-plugin admission path.\n72\t- HLR-2 (P0, supporting): PyTorchJobs correctly enter and release per-project\n73\t  GPU quota through the group-based admission, completion, and requeue.\n74\t\n75\t## Branch Context\n76\t\n77\t- Branch B of the gang-admission semantics investigation: applies when\n78\t  scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue is required. If Kueue-native semantics are\n79\t  sufficient, this epic is removed. Serial after the coscheduling integration\n80\t  work — the operator adaptation builds against the group mechanism it\n81\t  produces.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99416dc38feb6afb","agent_id":"a2a7cb73cc5c9b3e4","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"ebeb749a-2ac7-4084-a54c-295d5d9bf2fb","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:14:16.291Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1ce78364e0f095b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept",