e Correctness (1/2)\n94\tAll three Investigations genuinely change downstream structure: E001 selects Branch A vs\n95\tBranch B (rewrites E006/E007 and determines branch existence), E002 rewrites E005's scope,\n96\tE003 determines E007's existence. All Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts. All\n97\tepics with `gated_by` set have `gate_failure_impact` with both `action` and\n98\t`fallback_approach` populated, and every `gated_by` target appears in that epic's direct\n99\t`dependencies`.\n100\tIssue (gating metadata): E007 lists Investigation E001 in `dependencies` and the DAG\n101\tjustification states the E001 outcome \"may rewrite integration approach,\" yet `gated_by`\n102\tnames only E003 — the E001 rewrite-gate effect on E007 is not recorded in gate metadata.\n103\tSince `gated_by` is single-valued, one of E007's two Investigation dependencies is\n104\tungated; the scheduling edge is present and existence gating is recorded, so execution is\n105\tnot incorrect, but the rewrite-on-outcome-B path is invisible to gate consumers.\n106\t\n107\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n108\tType-appropriate signal fields throughout: E001-E003 (Investigation) carry\n109\t`investigation_signals`; all Implementation epics, including branch epics, carry the\n110\t9-signal `ai_signals`. Frontmatter values match the ai-signals rationale files exactly for\n111\tall 12 epics. Signal values are consistent with strategy content and the architecture\n112\tcontext: E002's `human_judgment_required: -2` matches the stakeholder-dependent preemption\n113\tdecision; E007's `existing_foundation: 0` / `pattern_precedent: 0` match the Tech Preview\n114\tstatus; BE011's `pattern_precedent: -1` matches \"Volcano is not shipped or supported.\"\n115\tMinor: BRANCH-A-E008's `architecture_claims: 1` rationale asserts the architecture context\n116\tdocuments \"both job types' Kueue integrations\"; the context file documents PyTorchJob\n117\tadmission via Kueue integration and lists RayCluster/RayJob CRDs as interfaces, but does\n118\tnot explicitly document RayJob's Kueue admission integration — the claim is slightly\n119\toverstated.\n120\t\n121\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n122\tEvery epic has testable ACs with concrete measurement approaches. Rule-mandated ACs\n123\tverified: the konflux chain coupling is carried by BE011's \"Konflux build pipeline ...\n124\tgreen for the revision being integrated\" AC (Rule 25), and no replacement or docs-authoring\n125\tepics exist to mandate rollback/doc-review ACs. No epic body references sibling epics by\n126\tdraft ID — all cross-references use descriptive names (\"the gang-admission semantics\n127\tinvestigation\").\n128\tMinor: E004's fourth AC (\"a pending job admitted when quota frees up starts with all its\n129\tpods ... consistent with the all-or-nothing admission requirement\") verifies behavior\n130\tdelivered by the gated branch admission work, which sits outside E004's dependency\n131\tclosure; as written it cannot be verified until gang admission lands.\n132\t\n133\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n134\tAll strategy scope is covered: piecemeal admission (HLR-1), quota (HLR-2), Dashboard\n135\tvisibility (HLR-3), preemption (HLR-4), topology-aware placement (HLR-5), and all three\n136\topen questions have owners. Out-of-scope boundaries (GPU sharing, multi-cluster queueing)\n137\tare respected. The conditional branches cover both bounded outcomes of OQ1 (Kueue\n138\tsufficient vs scheduler-plugin required), and the remaining open questions use true gates\n139\t(rewrite/remove) on main-plan epics, faithfully representing the strategy's statement that\n140\tOQ1's answer \"changes the shape of most implementation work.\" The strategy has no\n141\tPrerequisites & Process Gates section declaring documentation support, so no docs-authoring\n142\tepic is required. Health warnings preserve the strategy-level risks (P2 priority inversion\n143\trisk, Tech Preview scope trap, shared config surface).\n144\tMinor: Branch B includes a dedicated Training Operator adaptation epic (BRANCH-B-E012)\n145\tbecause operator-created pods must carry pod-group membership, but no KubeRay/RayJob-side\n146\tcounterpart is scoped, even though BE011's scope and AC claim RayJob workloads move \"from\n147\tpending ... to fully admitted as single units.\" Whether RayJob pod group membership can be\n148\tinjected by the BE011 integration (e.g. admission-time wiring) or requires KubeRay\n149\tadaptation is unaddressed — the RayJob path under Branch B is thinner than the symmetric\n150\tPyTorchJob path.\n151\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a632f260cbe55724","agent_id":"a2f7dab5f8f492a80","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"d636c3cf-1e41-400b-b8c6-8a8fb06ea50c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:24:22.769Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8134af5b8f49d204","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
