on | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, BRANCH-B-E011 |\n89\t\n90\tBranch DAG:\n91\t\n92\t```mermaid\n93\tgraph TD\n94\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9005-E001] --> AE008[BRANCH-A-E008 Kueue gang admission config]\n95\t    E001 --> AE009[BRANCH-A-E009 Training Operator conformance]\n96\t    E001 --> BE008[BRANCH-B-E008 repo onboarding]\n97\t    E001 --> BE009[BRANCH-B-E009 license validation]\n98\t    BE008 --> BE010[BRANCH-B-E010 konflux onboarding]\n99\t    BE009 --> BE011[BRANCH-B-E011 coscheduling integration]\n100\t    BE011 --> BE012[BRANCH-B-E012 Training Operator adaptation]\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\tNote: no edge BRANCH-B-E010 → BRANCH-B-E011 — konflux onboarding and the\n104\tintegration implementation run in parallel (Rule 10); the coupling is enforced by\n105\ta \"build pipeline green\" acceptance criterion on the integration epic (Rule 25).\n106\t\n107\tThe two other open questions use true gates on main-plan epics rather than\n108\tbranches: the preemption epic exists under either semantics outcome (E002 gates\n109\tE005 with `rewrite`), and topology placement exists only under the maturity\n110\toutcome (E003 gates E007 with `remove` — under the negative outcome HLR-5 is\n111\tdeferred and no branch work exists, so a single gated main-plan epic is the\n112\tfaithful representation).\n113\t\n114\t## DAG Justification\n115\t\n116\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n117\t|------|------|-----------|\n118\t| E001 → E006 | Rule 3 | Admission-state and queue-position surfacing depends on which admission mechanism is selected; investigation outcome rewrites the Dashboard's data sources. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n119\t| E004 → E006 | Rule 13 | Dashboard builds against the per-project quota model produced by the quota implementation (consumes its API/CR surface). |\n120\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 | Preemption semantics (full eviction vs checkpoint-aware) determine the epic's scope/approach. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n121\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 3 | Topology placement epic