{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af6241d02f2cda75","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008\n3\ttitle: Enable and validate Kueue-native gang admission for training queues\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the gang-admission semantics investigation requires scheduler-plugin\n16\t    work beyond Kueue, this epic is removed and the coscheduling-based branch applies.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 7\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Enable and validate Kueue-native gang admission for training queues\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tBranch A (Kueue's current gang-admission semantics are sufficient): configures\n38\tand validates all-or-nothing admission via Kueue for multi-node training\n39\tworkloads — PyTorchJob and RayJob — so a job holds zero GPUs until all of its\n40\tpods can be admitted, eliminating the piecemeal occupation and partial-timeout\n41\tfailures described in the strategy.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Configure the platform's Kueue queueing layer so training queues admit\n46\t  multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads all-or-nothing (gang admission via\n47\t  waitForPodsReady semantics), consistent with the validation performed in the\n48\t  gang-admission semantics investigation.\n49\t- Cover both job types' admission paths (PyTorchJob via the training-operator\n50\t  Kueue integration, RayJob via the Kuberay/Kueue integration).\n51\t- Tune admission behavior at target scale per the investigation's findings\n52\t  (queue depth, contention, timeout and requeue handling for jobs that cannot\n53\t  be fully admitted).\n54\t- Coordinate with the per-project GPU quota configuration, which shares the\n55\t  same Kueue queueing objects, so quota and gang semantics compose correctly.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A pending multi-node PyTorchJob or RayJob holds zero GPUs while waiting for\n60\t  its remaining pods, measured by per-job GPU allocation during the pending\n61\t  window across a representative-scale test run.\n62\t- A job that cannot be fully admitted within its timeout is rejected/evicted as\n63\t  a whole unit with its quota released, measured by no lingering partial\n64\t  allocation after timeout.\n65\t- Under contention (multiple teams' jobs competing for one GPU pool), admission\n66\t  remains all-or-nothing and quota accounting is correct, measured by admission\n67\t  events and GPU allocation over the contention window.\n68\t- Behavior matches the gang-admission semantics investigation's recommendation\n69\t  (the configuration implements the validated semantics, not an assumption).\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing; no partial\n74\t  GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods.\n75\t\n76\t## Branch Context\n77\t\n78\t- Branch A of the gang-admission semantics investigation: applies when\n79\t  Kueue-native semantics are judged sufficient at target scale. If the\n80\t  investigation instead requires scheduler-plugin work, this epic is removed and\n81\t  the coscheduling integration path applies.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a632f260cbe55724","agent_id":"a2f7dab5f8f492a80","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"aab76c97-938d-424b-ba30-abe9ce