discovery (Tech Preview) maturity for topology-aware placement | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E004 | Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission time across training job types | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E005 | Implement admin-defined preemption policy for higher-priority training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E006 | Surface queue position, quota consumption, and admission state for pending jobs in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n40\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E007 | Prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes for training job placement | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n41\t\n42\t`epic_count` counts main-plan epics (7). Branch epics (7, below) are plan documents\n43\tattached to the gating investigation, not standalone issues.\n44\t\n45\t## Dependency DAG\n46\t\n47\tMain plan (arrows point from dependency to dependent):\n48\t\n49\t```mermaid\n50\tgraph TD\n51\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9005-E001 gang admission investigation] --> E006[RHAISTRAT-9005-E006 Dashboard visibility]\n52\t    E004[RHAISTRAT-9005-E004 GPU quota at admission] --> E006\n53\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-9005-E002 preemption semantics investigation] --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9005-E005 preemption policy]\n54\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-9005-E003 topology maturity investigation] --> E007[RHAISTRAT-9005-E007 topology-aware placement]\n55\t    E001 --> E007\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\tBranch epics are excluded from the main-plan critical path. Main-plan critical\n59\tpath length: 2 (e.g. E001 → E006).\n60\t\n61\t## Conditional Decomposition Branches\n62\t\n63\tOpen Question 1 (\"do Kueue's current gang-admission semantics satisfy HLR-1 at\n64\ttarget scale, or is scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue needed?\") has two bounded\n65\toutcomes, and the strategy itself states the answer \"changes the shape of most\n66\timplementation work\". The admission implementation is therefore decomposed into\n67\tconditional branches gated by E001:\n68\t\n69\t- **Branch A — Kueue semantics sufficient**: configuration and validation of\n70\t  Kueue-native all-or-nothing admission (`waitForPodsReady`) for PyTorchJob and\n71\t  RayJob queues, plus Training Operator conformance work.\n72\t- **Branch B — scheduler-plugin work required**: the coscheduling scheduler\n73\t  plugin is not in the platform inventory (architecture context ships no\n74\t  scheduler plugins; Volcano is explicitly not shipped), so this branch carries\n75\t  the full new-component onboarding chain (repo-onboarding ∥ license-validation\n76\t  → konflux-onboarding ∥ integration implementation → Training Operator\n77\t  adaptation).\n78\t\n79\tBranch epic files:\n80\t\n81\t| File | Branch | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Dependencies |\n82\t|------|--------|-------|------|------|----------|--------------|\n83\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008.md | A | Enable and validate Kueue-native gang admission for training queues | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n84\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E009.md | A | Training Operator conformance with Kueue-native gang admission at scale | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n85\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E008.md | B | Midstream repo onboarding for the coscheduling scheduler plugin | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n86\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E009.md | B | License validation for the coscheduling scheduler plugin dependency tree | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001 |\n87\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E010.md | B | Konflux onboarding for the coscheduling scheduler plugin | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, BRANCH-B-E008 |\n88\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E011.md | B | Integrate coscheduling-based gang admission for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, BRANCH-B-E009 |\n89\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E012.md | B | Adapt Training Operator jobs to coscheduling-based gang admission | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | E001, BRANCH-B-E011 |\n90\t\n91\tBranch DAG:\n92\t\n93\t```mermaid\n94\tgraph TD\n95\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9005-E001] --> AE008[BRANCH-A-E008 Kueue gang admission config]\n96\t    E001 --> AE009[BRANCH-A-E009 Training Operator conformance]\n97\t    E001 --> BE008[BRANCH-B-E008 repo onboarding]\n98\t    E001 --> BE009[BRANCH-B-E009 license validation]\n99\t    BE008 --> BE010[BRANCH-B-E010 konflux onboarding]\n100\t    BE009 --> BE011[BRANCH-B-E011 coscheduling integration]\n101\t    BE011 --> BE012[BRANCH-B-E012 Training Operator adaptation]\n102\t```\n103\t\n104\tNote: no edge BRANCH-B-E010 → BRANCH-B-E011 — konflux onboarding and the\n105\tintegration implementation run in parallel (Rule 10); the coupling is enforced by\n106\ta \"build pipeline green\" acceptance criterion on the integration epic (Rule 25).\n107\t\n108\tRayJob pod-group membership under Branch B is delivered by the integration\n109\tepic's (BRANCH-B-E011) admission-time wiring on KubeRay-created pods — KubeRay\n110\tis part of the Distributed Workloads component, so no separate KubeRay\n111\tonboarding or adaptation epic is scoped. A KubeRay adaptation work item is spun\n112\tout under that component only if the admission-time wiring cannot attach group\n113\tmembership to KubeRay-created pods; the PyTorchJob path is not blocked by that\n114\tcontingency.\n115\t\n116\tThe two other open questions use true gates on main-plan epics rather than\n117\tbranches: the preemption epic exists under either semantics outcome (E002 gates\n118\tE005 with `rewrite`), and topology placement exists only under the maturity\n119\toutcome (E003 gates E007 with `remove` — under the negative outcome HLR-5 is\n120\tdeferred and no branch work exists, so a single gated main-plan epic is the\n121\tfaithful representation).\n122\t\n123\t## DAG Justification\n124\t\n125\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n126\t|------|------|-----------|\n127\t| E001 → E006 | Ru