ueueing/quota, which stays in Kueue). Investigations are independent of each other and of quota work. |\n139\t| BRANCH-A-E008 ∥ BRANCH-A-E009 | Rule 14 | Different repos (Kueue config vs training-operator), no shared artifacts. BRANCH-A-E009 stands up its own test-scoped queue configuration for validation (as the investigation harness did) and does not consume BRANCH-A-E008's product queue configuration. |\n140\t\n141\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n142\t\n143\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n144\t|-----|----------|-------|\n145\t| HLR-1 (all-or-nothing admission) | P0 | E001 (investigation); BRANCH-A-E008 + BRANCH-A-E009 (outcome A) or BRANCH-B-E008/E009/E010/E011/E012 (outcome B) |\n146\t| HLR-2 (per-project GPU quota at admission) | P0 | E004 (quota enforcement; all-or-nothing admission of quota-admitted jobs is validated by the HLR-1 branch work) |\n147\t| HLR-3 (Dashboard queue/quota/admission visibility) | P1 | E006 |\n148\t| HLR-4 (preemption per admin policy) | P1 | E002 (investigation), E005 |\n149\t| HLR-5 (topology-aligned placement) | P2 | E003 (investigation), E007 |\n150\t\n151\tAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements.\n152\t\n153\t## Health Warnings\n154\t\n155\t- **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table,\n156\t  Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then), or NFRs. Team ownership was inferred\n157\t  from architecture context; epic acceptance criteria were derived from HLRs and\n158\t  may need refinement against the strategy author's intent.\n159\t- **Priority inversion risk**: HLR-5 (topology-aligned placement) is P2 despite\n160\t  the problem statement citing \"significant throughput loss\" from mis-topologized\n161\t  placement. If field reports weigh heavily, consider raising it; it is also the\n162\t  requirement most at risk of deferral (Tech Preview dependency).\n163\t- **Scope trap**: HLR-5's acceptance depends on node topology discovery\n164\t  infrastructure that is only Tech Preview — building a P2 feature on Tech