{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a96e17de5d992c22","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate Kueue gang-admission semantics at target scale for PyTorchJob and\n4\t  RayJob\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n6\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n7\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Validate Kueue gang-admission semantics at target scale for PyTorchJob and RayJob\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolves the strategy's first open question: whether Kueue's current gang-admission\n31\tsemantics (all-or-nothing admission via `waitForPodsReady`) actually satisfy the\n32\tall-or-nothing requirement for multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads at the\n33\tplatform's target scale, or whether scheduler-plugin work (e.g. a coscheduling\n34\tplugin) beyond Kueue is required. The outcome determines which implementation\n35\tpath the rest of the queue-aware scheduling work takes.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Reproduce the piecemeal-admission failure mode described in the strategy\n40\t  (partial GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods, timeout deaths of\n41\t  partially scheduled jobs) with multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads\n42\t  under Kueue admission.\n43\t- Exercise Kueue's all-or-nothing admission (`waitForPodsReady`) for both job\n44\t  types at representative scale (job sizes and queue depth matching customer\n45\t  fleets, e.g. 16-GPU multi-node jobs), including contention scenarios where\n46\t  multiple teams' jobs compete for the same GPU pool.\n47\t- Determine whether admission semantics hold at target scale: no partial GPU\n48\t  occupation during pending admission, correct release of quota on eviction or\n49\t  timeout, and re-admission behavior after preemption or failure.\n50\t- Produce a written recommendation with a clear decision: (A) Kueue-native\n51\t  semantics are sufficient, or (B) scheduler-plugin work (e.g. coscheduling)\n52\t  beyond Kueue is required — including the evidence (metrics, logs, test\n53\t  results) supporting the decision.\n54\t- Identify any Kueue configuration or integration gaps discovered along the way\n55\t  that either outcome would need to address.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A test harness exists that submits multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads\n60\t  through Kueue queues and observes admission behavior at representative scale.\n61\t- For each job type, it is demonstrated and documented whether pending jobs hold\n62\t  zero GPUs until all pods can be admitted (pass) or occupy GPUs partially\n63\t  while waiting (fail).\n64\t- A written recommendation selects outcome A or B with supporting evidence and\n65\t  identifies the concrete consequences for the admission, quota, preemption,\n66\t  topology, and Dashboard work.\n67\t- If outcome B, the recommendation identifies the scheduler-plugin approach to\n68\t  carry forward (component to onboard, integration points with Kueue queueing).\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-1 (P0): this investigation determines whether Kueue-native semantics\n73\t  satisfy the all-or-nothing admission requirement or whether scheduler-plugin\n74\t  work is needed.\n75\t\n76\t## Open Questions Addressed\n77\t\n78\t- Strategy Open Question 1 (Kueue gang-admission semantics vs scheduler-plugin\n79\t  work at target scale).\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97582f8c6f1245c2","agent_id":"a840909f53461e0a9","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82