{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-902ab671d9a203ae","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E002\n3\ttitle: Determine required preemption semantics and checkpoint overhead for training\n4\t  workloads\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n6\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n7\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -3\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Determine required preemption semantics and checkpoint overhead for training workloads\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolves the strategy's third open question: what preemption semantics reference\n31\tcustomers actually need — full eviction with requeue, or checkpoint-aware\n32\tgraceful preemption. Field signals are conflicting and there is no benchmark of\n33\tcheckpoint overhead. The outcome determines the implementation approach for the\n34\tadmin-defined preemption policy.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Gather and reconcile the conflicting field signals from reference customers\n39\t  about preemption expectations (what may be preempted, what must survive,\n40\t  expected requeue behavior).\n41\t- Benchmark checkpoint overhead for representative multi-node GPU training jobs\n42\t  (checkpoint frequency, size, duration, and the resulting throughput loss) to\n43\t  quantify the cost of checkpoint-aware graceful preemption versus full eviction.\n44\t- Determine whether existing workload frameworks (PyTorchJob, RayJob) support\n45\t  the checkpoint/resume hooks that checkpoint-aware graceful preemption would\n46\t  require.\n47\t- Produce a written recommendation selecting the preemption semantics\n48\t  (full eviction with requeue, or checkpoint-aware graceful preemption, or a\n49\t  policy-configurable mix) with the supporting customer input and benchmark\n50\t  data, and the consequences for the preemption policy implementation.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Reference-customer preemption requirements are documented, with conflicting\n55\t  signals reconciled into a single recommendation.\n56\t- Checkpoint overhead is benchmarked for representative training jobs and the\n57\t  numbers are recorded (duration, size, throughput impact).\n58\t- A written recommendation selects the preemption semantics and states what the\n59\t  preemption policy implementation must support.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-4 (P1): this investigation determines the semantics the admin-defined\n64\t  preemption policy must implement.\n65\t\n66\t## Open Questions Addressed\n67\t\n68\t- Strategy Open Question 3 (preemption semantics: full eviction with requeue vs\n69\t  checkpoint-aware graceful preemption; checkpoint overhead benchmark).\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97582f8c6f1245c2","agent_id":"a840909f53461e0a9","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"dbe0658d-23dc-49a6-9ae7-8f7534d12829","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:30:03.549Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-902ab671d9a203ae","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
