{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-915c4a873f23a020","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n3\ttitle: Assess node topology discovery (Tech Preview) maturity for topology-aware placement\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 0\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Assess node topology discovery (Tech Preview) maturity for topology-aware placement\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's second open question: whether the node topology\n30\tdiscovery capability that topology-aware placement depends on — currently Tech\n31\tPreview — is mature enough to build on in this release. The outcome determines\n32\twhether the topology-aligned placement requirement is implemented now or\n33\tdeferred.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Inventory the current state of node topology discovery (API surface, known\n38\t  defects, upgrade history, scale limits) from release notes, upstream\n39\t  repositories, and the platform's Tech Preview documentation.\n40\t- Validate discovery behavior on representative cluster nodes (does reported\n41\t  topology — e.g. NVLink domains — match actual hardware topology?).\n42\t- Identify known blockers or deprecations that would break topology-aligned\n43\t  placement within this release's support window.\n44\t- Produce a written go/no-go recommendation: build topology-aware placement on\n45\t  Tech Preview discovery this release, or defer the requirement to a release\n46\t  where the foundation is GA.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- The maturity assessment documents the discovery capability's API stability,\n51\t  defect history, and scale limits with references.\n52\t- Discovery behavior is validated on representative hardware and the results\n53\t  are recorded.\n54\t- A written go/no-go recommendation is produced, including the risks of building\n55\t  on Tech Preview foundations if the recommendation is go.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-5 (P2): this investigation determines whether topology-aware placement\n60\t  can be built this release or must be deferred.\n61\t\n62\t## Open Questions Addressed\n63\t\n64\t- Strategy Open Question 2 (is Tech Preview node topology discovery mature\n65\t  enough to build on this release?).\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97582f8c6f1245c2","agent_id":"a840909f53461e0a9","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"80c71ace-4852-40e8-bf60-f92a0d707adb","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:30:04.731Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-915c4a873f23a020","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
