{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84e3ff93f4a4ecb5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E004\n3\ttitle: Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission time across training job types\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission time across training job types\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDelivers per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission time, so that a project's\n34\tpending training jobs (PyTorchJob and RayJob) cannot consume more GPUs than the\n35\tproject's quota allows, regardless of job type. Enforcement happens at admission\n36\t(pending jobs hold no resources), building on the platform's Kueue-based\n37\tqueueing layer.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Define the per-project GPU quota model on top of the existing Kueue\n42\t  queueing primitives (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model), mapping projects to\n43\t  quota boundaries so quota is shared across PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads\n44\t  within a project.\n45\t- Implement/administer the quota configuration so that admission-time checks\n46\t  reject or delay jobs that would exceed a project's GPU quota.\n47\t- Ensure quota is correctly released when jobs complete, fail, or are evicted,\n48\t  including under the all-or-nothing admission semantics delivered by the\n49\t  gang-admission work (the two share Kueue queueing configuration; coordinate\n50\t  the configuration changes rather than duplicating them).\n51\t- Verify quota accounting across mixed fleets of PyTorchJob and RayJob\n52\t  workloads in the same project, including concurrent multi-node jobs.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A project submitting training jobs whose combined GPU requests exceed its\n57\t  quota has the excess jobs held pending at admission (zero GPUs occupied),\n58\t  measured by pending workloads and GPU allocation per project over the test\n59\t  window.\n60\t- Quota is enforced uniformly across PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads in the\n61\t  same project (a RayJob cannot bypass a quota saturated by PyTorchJobs, and\n62\t  vice versa).\n63\t- Quota is fully released within a bounded time after job completion, failure,\n64\t  or eviction, measured by post-job GPU allocation returning to the pre-job\n65\t  level.\n66\t- When quota frees up (job completion, failure, or eviction), a pending job\n67\t  that fits within the freed quota is admitted within a bounded time, measured\n68\t  by the time from the quota-release event to the job's admission event. This\n69\t  criterion verifies quota-release timing only; whether the admitted job then\n70\t  starts with all its pods is the all-or-nothing admission behavior delivered\n71\t  by the gang-admission work selected by the admission-semantics investigation,\n72\t  and is verified there as a composition check with this epic's quota\n73\t  configuration.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-2 (P0): per-project GPU quota enforced at admission time across training\n78\t  job types (PyTorchJob, RayJob).\n79\t- Supports HLR-1 (P0): quota-enforced admission keeps pending jobs\n80\t  resource-free; all-or-nothing admission itself is delivered by the\n81\t  gang-admission work selected by the admission-semantics investigation.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97582f8c6f1245c2","agent_id":"a840909f53461e0a9","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"fec10f38-4633-4369-b9fd-cf3a8b5d980b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:30:09.095Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84e3ff93f4a4ecb5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
