{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98fd62d8ef9183a1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E005\n3\ttitle: Implement admin-defined preemption policy for higher-priority training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation selects checkpoint-aware graceful preemption\n15\t    instead of full eviction with requeue, this epic's scope is rewritten to include\n16\t    checkpoint/resume coordination (and Training Operator scope is added); the preemption\n17\t    policy itself is still delivered.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Implement admin-defined preemption policy for higher-priority training workloads\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tDelivers preemption of lower-priority training workloads by higher-priority ones\n40\taccording to an admin-defined policy. The concrete preemption semantics (full\n41\teviction with requeue, or checkpoint-aware graceful preemption) are determined\n42\tby the preemption-semantics investigation; this epic implements the policy\n43\tmachinery on the platform's Kueue-based queueing layer once that outcome is\n44\tknown.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Implement admin-defined preemption policy configuration on the queueing\n49\t  layer, allowing administrators to express which workloads may preempt which\n50\t  (workload priority and queue boundaries).\n51\t- Implement the preemption semantics selected by the preemption-semantics\n52\t  investigation: full eviction with requeue, checkpoint-aware graceful\n53\t  preemption, or a policy-configurable mix — including the requeue/admission\n54\t  path for preempted jobs.\n55\t- Ensure preempted quota is released promptly so the preempting workload can be\n56\t  admitted, and preempted jobs re-enter the queue rather than being lost.\n57\t- If checkpoint-aware graceful preemption is selected, coordinate with the\n58\t  Training Operator on checkpoint/suspend support (the operator-side work will\n59\t  be scoped when the semantics decision lands; this epic covers the\n60\t  queueing-layer policy and lifecycle).\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- An administrator can define a preemption policy, and a higher-priority\n65\t  workload submitted against a saturated GPU pool causes a lower-priority\n66\t  workload to be preempted per that policy, measured by admission events and GPU\n67\t  reallocation within the test window.\n68\t- Preempted workloads are requeued (and, if the selected semantics require it,\n69\t  resumed from checkpoint) rather than lost, measured by their eventual\n70\t  re-admission.\n71\t- GPU quota held by the preempted workload is released to the preempting\n72\t  workload within a bounded time, measured by GPU allocation transitions.\n73\t- Preemption behavior matches the semantics recommended by the\n74\t  preemption-semantics investigation.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-4 (P1): higher-priority workloads can preempt lower-priority ones\n79\t  according to an admin-defined policy.\n80\t\n81\t## Dependencies and Gates\n82\t\n83\t- Gated by the preemption-semantics investigation (customer-requirements\n84\t  reconciliation plus checkpoint-overhead benchmark): if the outcome differs\n85\t  from the assumed approach, this epic's scope is rewritten rather than\n86\t  removed — preemption is delivered under either semantics.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97582f8c6f1245c2","agent_id":"a840909f53461e0a9","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"647e1e1f-d6b9-4991-9c42-420dd77797e7","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:30:10.164Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98fd62d8ef9183a1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
