{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c4ca619dade3a76","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E007\n3\ttitle: Prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes for training job placement\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: 'Primary gate (topology-discovery maturity, action: remove):\n16\t    if node topology discovery is not mature enough this release, HLR-5 is deferred\n17\t    and this epic is removed; the limitation is documented for customers. Second gate\n18\t    (gang-admission semantics, action: rewrite): if the investigation selects scheduler-plugin\n19\t    work beyond Kueue, this epic is retained but its integration approach is rewritten\n20\t    to compose topology preference with the coscheduling-based admission mechanism\n21\t    instead of Kueue-native admission.'\n22\tai_signals:\n23\t  change_specificity: 0\n24\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n25\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n26\t  existing_foundation: 0\n27\t  open_questions: -1\n28\t  external_dependency: 0\n29\t  human_process_gates: 0\n30\t  repo_access: 1\n31\t  architecture_claims: 1\n32\timplementation_type: null\n33\tinvestigation_signals: null\n34\tai_implementability: Medium\n35\tai_implementability_score: 1\n36\tjira_key: null\n37\tbranch: null\n38\t---\n39\t# Prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes for training job placement\n40\t\n41\t## Description\n42\t\n43\tDelivers placement that prefers GPU-topology-aligned nodes for training jobs\n44\twhen the cluster exposes topology information (e.g. keeping a job's GPUs within\n45\tNVLink domains), addressing the throughput loss customers report from\n46\tmis-topologized placement. Only proceeds if the node topology discovery\n47\tfoundation is judged mature enough for this release.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Implement a placement preference for training jobs that uses cluster topology\n52\t  information (when exposed) to prefer topology-aligned node/GPU sets for a\n53\t  job's pods.\n54\t- Integrate the preference with the admission mechanism selected by the\n55\t  gang-admission semantics investigation, so topology preference applies at\n56\t  admission time without breaking all-or-nothing semantics.\n57\t- Degrade gracefully on clusters that do not expose topology information:\n58\t  placement falls back to the default behavior and the requirement's\n59\t  \"can prefer\" semantics are preserved.\n60\t- Validate placement quality (jobs land within aligned topology domains when\n61\t  available) and the throughput benefit on representative multi-node GPU jobs.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- On a cluster exposing topology information, admitted multi-node training jobs\n66\t  are placed on topology-aligned node/GPU sets when such sets are available,\n67\t  measured by comparing job pod placement against reported topology domains.\n68\t- On a cluster without topology information, jobs are admitted and placed via\n69\t  the default behavior with no errors, measured by admission success rate\n70\t  matching the non-topology baseline.\n71\t- Topology preference does not break all-or-nothing admission (no partial\n72\t  admission while waiting for a topology-aligned set), measured by GPU\n73\t  occupation of pending jobs remaining zero.\n74\t- A representative multi-node job shows no cross-domain GPU placement where an\n75\t  in-domain placement was available, measured over the validation run.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- HLR-5 (P2): job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the\n80\t  cluster exposes topology information.\n81\t\n82\t## Dependencies and Gates\n83\t\n84\t- Gated by the topology-discovery maturity investigation (primary gate,\n85\t  `remove`): if the Tech Preview discovery foundation is not mature enough for\n86\t  this release, this epic is removed and the requirement is deferred\n87\t  (documented limitation).\n88\t- Also gated by the gang-admission semantics investigation (second gate,\n89\t  `rewrite`): its outcome determines the admission mechanism the placement\n90\t  preference integrates with. Under the Kueue-sufficient outcome the preference\n91\t  composes with Kueue-native gang admission; under the scheduler-plugin outcome\n92\t  the integration approach is rewritten to compose with the coscheduling-based\n93\t  admission mechanism. Both gates are recorded in the gate-failure metadata\n94\t  above.\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97582f8c6f1245c2","agent_id":"a840909f53461e0a9","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"f68dbb91-95f6-4b5e-84e3-09ca571c7179","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:30:12.492Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c4ca619dade3a76","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
