admitted together).\n50\t- Fix Training Operator defects surfaced by that validation (e.g. incorrect\n51\t  suspend/resume handling, pod mutations that break admission, stuck jobs after\n52\t  partial-node failures), staying within the operator's existing\n53\t  Kueue-integration model.\n54\t- Ensure preempted/requeued PyTorchJobs restart correctly through the\n55\t  operator's suspend path when workload queueing is enabled.\n56\t- Stand up its own test-scoped Kueue queue configuration for the validation\n57\t  (separate queues, as the gang-admission semantics investigation's harness\n58\t  did), rather than consuming the product queue configuration: this epic runs\n59\t  in parallel with the Kueue-native gang-admission configuration work in the\n60\t  same branch (different repos, no shared artifacts), so the validation must\n61\t  not depend on that configuration landing first.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- Multi-node PyTorchJobs are admitted as whole units (launcher and all workers)\n66\t  through Kueue queueing, measured by admission events showing no partial pod\n67\t  sets running while a job is pending.\n68\t- A suspended-then-resumed PyTorchJob (pending → admitted, and preempted →\n69\t  requeued → re-admitted) completes training correctly, measured by job success\n70\t  over a test run exercising those transitions.\n71\t- No Training Operator defects remain that break all-or-nothing admission at\n72\t  representative scale, measured by the validation suite passing at the scale\n73\t  exercised in the gang-admission semantics investigation.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing — Training\n78\t  Operator side (PyTorchJob) of the Kueue-native admission path.\n79\t- HLR-2 (P0, supporting): PyTorchJobs correctly enter and release per-project\n80\t  GPU quota through admission, completion, and requeue.\n81\t\n82\t## Branch Context\n83\t\n84\t- Branch A of the gang-admission semantics investigation: applies when\n85\t  Kueue-native semantics are judged sufficient. If the investigation instead\n86\t  requires scheduler-plugin work, this epic is removed and the operator\n87\t  adaptation for coscheduling-based admission applies.\n88\t- Runs in parallel with the Kueue-native gang-admission configuration work\n89\t  (different repos); the validation above uses this epic's own test-scoped\n90\t  queue configuration and does not rely on the product queues that\n91\t  configuration sets up.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97582f8c6f1245c2","agent_id":"a840909f53461e0a9","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"b989fbb4-d9c5-4385-956b-29fc858a9f57","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:30:19.102Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac8a38628b732619","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
