r the upstream source and tags; document the fork's provenance and the\n51\t  upstream commit it is cut from.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A midstream repository exists under opendatahub-io containing the coscheduling\n56\t  scheduler plugin source at a documented upstream commit.\n57\t- The fork's branch structure and sync workflow are documented and match the\n58\t  platform's midstream conventions used by other queueing-layer components.\n59\t- The repository is accessible to the build/onboarding pipelines that follow.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-1 (P0, enabling): the scheduler plugin is the gang-admission foundation\n64\t  required to deliver all-or-nothing admission under this branch.\n65\t\n66\t## Branch Context\n67\t\n68\t- Branch B of the gang-admission semantics investigation: applies when\n69\t  scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue is required. If Kueue-native semantics are\n70\t  sufficient, this epic is removed.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97582f8c6f1245c2","agent_id":"a840909f53461e0a9","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"4df31314-d06b-4a16-9aa9-09cf60d9c90a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:30:20.302Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bb85f9b74130e5b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
