{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5f6ba656c4483b1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E011\n3\ttitle: Integrate coscheduling-based gang admission for training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E009\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If Kueue-native gang admission semantics are sufficient, this\n17\t    epic is removed.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: -1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 0\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 0\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Integrate coscheduling-based gang admission for training workloads\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tBranch B (scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue is required): integrates the\n39\tcoscheduling scheduler plugin into the platform's scheduling stack so that\n40\tmulti-node training workloads (PyTorchJob and RayJob) are admitted\n41\tall-or-nothing at the scheduler level, eliminating piecemeal GPU occupation and\n42\tpartial-timeout failures. Queueing and per-project quota remain on the\n43\tplatform's Kueue-based queueing layer; the plugin provides the pod-group gang\n44\tsemantics Kueue alone could not guarantee at target scale.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Integrate the coscheduling scheduler plugin with the cluster's scheduler\n49\t  configuration so pods carrying gang-scheduling groups (training job pods) are\n50\t  scheduled as whole units.\n51\t- Wire the plugin's pod-group semantics to the queueing layer's admission flow\n52\t  so PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads move from pending (zero GPUs held) to\n53\t  fully admitted as single units, including under contention and quota limits.\n54\t- Deliver RayJob-side pod-group membership through this integration's\n55\t  admission-time wiring: the integration ensures the pods KubeRay creates for a\n56\t  RayJob (RayCluster worker/ head pods) carry the gang-scheduling group\n57\t  membership the plugin requires (KubeRay is part of the Distributed Workloads\n58\t  component, so this wiring lands in the same component/team scope; no separate\n59\t  KubeRay onboarding is needed). If admission-time wiring cannot attach group\n60\t  membership to KubeRay-created pods, spin out a KubeRay adaptation work item\n61\t  under this component before the RayJob all-or-nothing acceptance criterion\n62\t  can be verified — the PyTorchJob path is not blocked by that contingency.\n63\t- Handle group timeout/eviction: a group that cannot be fully scheduled is\n64\t  rejected or evicted as a whole with quota released, and requeue behavior is\n65\t  preserved.\n66\t- Validate all-or-nothing behavior for both job types at the target scale\n67\t  exercised in the gang-admission semantics investigation.\n68\t\n69\t## Acceptance Criteria\n70\t\n71\t- A pending multi-node PyTorchJob or RayJob holds zero GPUs while waiting for\n72\t  its remaining pods, measured by per-job GPU allocation during the pending\n73\t  window across a representative-scale test run.\n74\t- A job group that cannot be fully scheduled within its timeout is evicted as a\n75\t  whole unit with quota released, measured by no lingering partial allocation\n76\t  after timeout.\n77\t- The Konflux build pipeline for the scheduler plugin is green for the revision\n78\t  being integrated, measured by the pipeline run status.\n79\t- Queueing and per-project quota continue to be enforced correctly with the\n80\t  plugin active, measured by admission events and per-project GPU allocation\n81\t  over the test window.\n82\t\n83\t## HLR Traceability\n84\t\n85\t- HLR-1 (P0): multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing; no partial\n86\t  GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods.\n87\t\n88\t## Branch Context\n89\t\n90\t- Branch B of the gang-admission semantics investigation: applies when\n91\t  scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue is required. If Kueue-native semantics are\n92\t  sufficient, this epic is removed. Serial after license validation (license\n93\t  failures would change the dependency set and the approach); parallel with the\n94\t  Konflux onboarding — the coupling is enforced by the green-pipeline\n95\t  acceptance criterion above, not a dependency edge.\n96\t- RayJob pod-group membership comes from this epic's admission-time wiring on\n97\t  KubeRay-created pods (see Scope), not from a separate KubeRay adaptation\n98\t  epic; a KubeRay adaptation work item is spun out only if that wiring cannot\n99\t  attach group membership.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97582f8c6f1245c2","agent_id":"a840909f53461e0a9","session_id":"b2cc3a11-1e81-4f82-9914-5f96aea9b357","uuid":"52cb1feb-239c-4bd7-a31b-816fd2cec996","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:30:26.908Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5f6ba656c4483b1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
